## SQ-ROLL-05 | Legendary Roll Medley servings by empty hand, dirt, chopsticks (medley at 155)
@group A
@commands `/setblock ~ ~ ~ roll_delight:legendary_roll_medley`; bot right-clicks with an empty hand 9 times, counting items; again with a held dirt block; then with chopsticks at hunger 10
@pass 3 mushroom slices, 3 Salmon Maki, 2 Tobiko in that order, then the plate stays (servings 0) and the 9th click breaks it for a bowl; held dirt places against it; chopsticks eat one serving in place, 1 damage (ROLL-10, ROLL-14, ROLL-18)
@fails `use` override, FeastBlock super
@from batches/r1102b/s3_A.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-16
> setblock 155 -60 500 roll_delight:legendary_roll_medley
> pbot spawn rl5 155 -60 503 minecraft:overworld survival
repeat 9
> pbot hold rl5 minecraft:air
> pbot use rl5 155 -60 500 up
> data get entity rl5 SelectedItem
> clear rl5
> data get block 155 -60 500
end
> execute if block 155 -60 500 minecraft:air run say ROLL05 medley gone after 9
> cdevtest items 155 -60 500 4 keep
> setblock 155 -60 500 roll_delight:legendary_roll_medley
> pbot hold rl5 minecraft:dirt
> pbot use rl5 155 -60 500 north
> execute if block 155 -60 499 minecraft:dirt run say ROLL05 dirt placed against the medley
> setblock 155 -60 499 minecraft:air
> pbot hunger rl5 10
> pbot hold rl5 roll_delight:chopsticks
> pbot use rl5 155 -60 500 up
> cdevtest player rl5
> cdevtest state 155 -60 500
> data get entity rl5 SelectedItem
expect ROLL05 medley gone after 9
expect ROLL05 dirt placed against the medley
expect verb=items items=\S*minecraft:bowl:1
expect verb=pbot\.hunger bot=rl5 food=10
expect verb=player name=rl5 .*food=(1[1-9]|20)
reject verb=pbot\.\S+ .*error=
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0
> pbot remove rl5
look the nine SelectedItem lines: 3 mushroom slices, 3 Salmon Maki, 2 Tobiko, then nothing (plate at servings 0), the 9th click breaks it (the bowl in the verb=items line); chopsticks: food above 10 in the verb=player line, the medley state one serving lower, SelectedItem Damage 1

